    <!-- ===================== CARD TEMPLATES ===================== -->
    <!--
      TAMIL-REVIEW

      From here to the end of the follow-up section, EVERY resource name is a key
      the `:domain` module emits as a `CopyRef`/`LineRef` (build plan §5.8). The
      names are not free: `CopyRes` maps each domain key to `R.string.<same name>`
      and `R.string.<same name>_en`, and `CopyResTest` fails the build if a key the
      domain can emit has no entry. Rename a string here and the test says so.

      The domain never emits prose — only these identifiers and numbers — which is
      why a banned word (CLAUDE.md #1) cannot reach a card through the domain. It
      can only get in *here*, which is why this file is scanned by
      checkBannedWords.
    -->
    <string name="card_differs_spoken_line">பேச்சில்: %1$s</string>
    <string name="card_differs_spoken_line_en">Said: %1$s</string>
    <string name="card_differs_written_line">ஆவணத்தில்: %1$s</string>
    <string name="card_differs_written_line_en">Document: %1$s</string>
    <string name="card_differs_footer">சரிபார்க்கவும்</string>
    <string name="card_differs_footer_en">Please check</string>

    <!--
      The small English line printed *under* the big Tamil pair on a DIFFERS card
      (§6.6 screen 3), so a reader who does not read Tamil can still follow the
      one fact on screen. It is English in both language modes by design — it has
      no `_en` sibling and `CopyRes` points both ids at this one string. In
      ENGLISH_ONLY mode the big lines are already English and the card simply does
      not draw this line; that is the card's decision, not a second resource.
    -->
    <string name="card_differs_english_small_line">Said: %1$s · Document: %2$s</string>

    <string name="card_not_in_document_spoken_line">அவர் சொன்னது: %1$s</string>
